Standardisation ensures Azure environments remain consistent regardless of which administrator or team deploys resources.

Areas commonly standardised include:

* Resource naming
* Tagging
* Security baselines
* Virtual network design
* Monitoring configuration
* Backup policies
* Documentation

# Real-Life Example:
For example, every production virtual machine may follow the same naming convention, security policy, monitoring configuration, and backup schedule.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is reducing configuration drift across hundreds of Azure subscriptions managed by different departments.

Standardisation simplifies administration and improves governance across large cloud environments.
